{"seq":1,"slug":"teaching-without-writing","title":"Teaching Without Writing","docCount":2,"url":"/c/people/socrates/major-works/teaching-without-writing","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-he-wrote-nothing","title":"为何不著一字","url":"/c/people/socrates/major-works/teaching-without-writing/why-he-wrote-nothing","wordCount":1863,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-socratic-problem","title":"苏格拉底问题","url":"/c/people/socrates/major-works/teaching-without-writing/the-socratic-problem","wordCount":1870,"readingTime":8}],"introMarkdown":"本章探讨苏格拉底\"不著一字\"这一独特现象。苏格拉底为何述而不作？这与他\"对话高于文字\"\"真理在于唤醒\"的哲学信念密切相关。然而，正因不著一字，我们对他的认识全赖他人各异的记述，从而产生了著名的\"苏格拉底问题\"——如何还原历史上真实的苏格拉底。本章揭示这一\"不著之著\"的深刻意味。\n"}